hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1736","\nNarrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ad-Dawraqiyy and Ziyad ibn Ayyub, they said: Narrated to us Isma'il, who reported from Ayyub.\n\nAlso narrated to us Muhammad ibn Bashshar, who said: Narrated to us 'Abd al-Wahhab, who said: Narrated to us Ayyub, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\Indeed"","" within the Friday (day) there is an hour in which"","" if a Muslim stands and prays"","" asking Allah for good in it"","" Allah will grant it to him.\""\n\nAnd he (the Prophet ﷺ) gestured with his hand"","" saying: \""It is a brief and fleeting moment.\""\n\nBundar said: And he gestured with his hand"","" saying: \""It is a brief and fleeting moment.\""\n\nWe (the narrators) said: \""It is a brief and fleeting moment.\""\n\nThere is no mention in the narration of Ibn 'Ulayyah of \""it to him\"" (i.e."","" the specific wording \""Allah will grant it to him\"" is not found in Ibn 'Ulayyah's narration)."""""
